      "content": "lol, you're still doing the goblin thing. i was hoping for a more serious, scientific answer.\n\ncan you please explain this without the fantasy metaphors? if a \"rogue\" strain or a different bacterium actually enters the culture, what is the biological process that allows it to take over? i'm specifically interested in how one species manages to outcompete the others so quickly—is it a matter of pH levels, nutrient acquisition, or something else entirely?",
